PUPPET BEATEN TO PULP

Los Angeles:  Police reportedly beat Howdy Doody to a pulp last night in
Hollywood.

"The little sap wouldn't stop talking," explained LAPD spokesman "Bull"
Conner.

The news comes in the wake of the recent incident where LA Police put
Charlie McCarthy through a chipper shredder.

The sudden wave of violence against formerly famous puppets and
ventriloquist dummies is seen as a safe outlet for the hostility of the
LA cops.  "Finally, they've found something they can brutalize without
violating their civil rights." said Jessie Jackson.

"It is obvious that the LA police have something against puppets and
marionettes," said Kukla, head of the Puppet Rights Association.  All
puppets have been urged to keep quiet in the presence of LA cops.  "They
seem to especially have a problem with wooden heads," Kukla added.

